                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cb9f59c3-31c9-457e-9490-e31aa9133f20",
                        "source_entry_id": "dd4dc59c-93aa-3158-808c-11d37ad59ce0",
                        "target_lang_word": "branch out",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "branch out",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41afe6d5-a352-3668-97b0-19313fb5e27a",
                                        "entry_id": "96c2d1c7-4cd6-37d7-ab03-aae6618abb78",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To expand in the manner of branches."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2507bf14-487e-422c-992f-e910d4a3a829",
                                                "sense_id": "41afe6d5-a352-3668-97b0-19313fb5e27a",
                                                "text": "The chart starts in the center and branches out from there."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c9dd4ac-e561-300a-92e5-41f8f4465e5d",
                                        "entry_id": "96c2d1c7-4cd6-37d7-ab03-aae6618abb78",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To expand one's interests or activities in a new direction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a7bca47-79f8-4632-a6a9-8272bc1e7022",
                                                "sense_id": "7c9dd4ac-e561-300a-92e5-41f8f4465e5d",
                                                "text": "Studying Latin may make it easier to branch out into Spanish or Italian."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c9e1bba-bdaa-48e9-98e4-277d502b9118",
                                                "sense_id": "7c9dd4ac-e561-300a-92e5-41f8f4465e5d",
                                                "text": "Once relegated to facelifts and fat reduction, medical tourism has branched out into almost every kind of procedure, including bypass surgery, heart-valve replacement, angioplasty, knee reconstruction, and spinal fusion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a33ba287-e55c-4a8c-bb03-c0c95985e9f7",
                                                "sense_id": "7c9dd4ac-e561-300a-92e5-41f8f4465e5d",
                                                "text": "Here's the briefest history of rail freight. The railways are conceived for moving coal. They do well at that and immediately branch out into other freight. They do quite well at that, too - after all, compared with a horse and cart, they are a revelation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c51d7ee9-a10e-3cf9-b5e9-8c84678f9e1c",
                                        "entry_id": "96c2d1c7-4cd6-37d7-ab03-aae6618abb78",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To white out or expand the whitespace around the title or other words, lines, etc. in a document."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0ec1f3e2-0067-4f2c-86a7-3852b96525b4",
                        "source_entry_id": "dd4dc59c-93aa-3158-808c-11d37ad59ce0",
                        "target_lang_word": "ramify",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ramify",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ada5548-1d67-3071-997c-67c6e0fa6a5a",
                                        "entry_id": "dbb05d61-76b4-30cd-ac1f-8dafb72ab022",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To divide into branches or subdivisions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16569f84-0e01-4b1c-bca8-2100003d30dc",
                                                "sense_id": "2ada5548-1d67-3071-997c-67c6e0fa6a5a",
                                                "text": "The cortical, hemispheral or superficial veins ramify on the surface of the brain and return the blood from the cortical substance into the venous sinuses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0b3c9f9-2d78-38ac-95d8-2c5d40667414",
                                        "entry_id": "dbb05d61-76b4-30cd-ac1f-8dafb72ab022",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spread or diversify into multiple fields or categories."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4af7be7-3b50-4cf7-80f6-dcf42eb3b788",
                                                "sense_id": "d0b3c9f9-2d78-38ac-95d8-2c5d40667414",
                                                "text": "to ramify an art, subject, scheme"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc896bf9-be13-4855-9c48-b880a1a16375",
                                                "sense_id": "d0b3c9f9-2d78-38ac-95d8-2c5d40667414",
                                                "text": "And, of course, on such momentous occasions as these, Manning was in his element. None knew those difficult ropes better than he; none used them with a more serviceable and yet discreet alacrity. In every juncture he had the right word, or the right silence; his influence ramified in all directions, from the Pope's audience chamber to the English Cabinet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f916060d-592f-47e0-8a0a-1686421af359",
                                                "sense_id": "d0b3c9f9-2d78-38ac-95d8-2c5d40667414",
